body:
When importing a ZIP archive with an existing filename, users now see a confirmation dialog offering to override or keep both files. Choosing "keep both" appends numeric suffixes (`file (1).zip`, `file (2).zip`, etc.).

## Changes

**File conflict detection**
- Extract and check filename before copying to internal storage
- Show dialog only when conflict exists

**Confirmation dialog**
- "Override" button replaces existing file
- "Keep Both" button generates unique filename with counter suffix
- Dialog is cancellable

**Unique filename generation**
- Preserves file extensions correctly: `my.archive.zip` → `my.archive (1).zip`
- Handles edge cases: hidden files (`.config`), no extension, trailing dots

## Implementation

```java
// Check for conflicts before copying
File targetFile = new File(internalDir, fileName);
if (targetFile.exists()) {
    showFileExistsDialog(uri, fileName);
} else {
    File internalFile = copyToInternalStorage(uri, fileName);
    checkAndPromptForPassword(internalFile);
}

// Generate unique names
private String generateUniqueFileName(String fileName) {
    String nameWithoutExt = fileName;
    String extension = "";
    int lastDotIndex = fileName.lastIndexOf('.');
    if (lastDotIndex > 0 && lastDotIndex < fileName.length() - 1) {
        nameWithoutExt = fileName.substring(0, lastDotIndex);
        extension = fileName.substring(lastDotIndex);
    }

    int counter = 1;
    String newFileName = fileName;
    while (new File(internalDir, newFileName).exists()) {
        newFileName = nameWithoutExt + " (" + counter + ")" + extension;
        counter++;
    }
    return newFileName;
}
```

String resources added for dialog UI (title, message, buttons).

